      <Output>
        <StdOut>Given I have an access token
-&gt; done: ApiSteps.Login() (0.0s)
And I have created a sensor
-&gt; done: ApiSteps.ExistingSensor() (0.0s)
When I register a consumption of 150 liters
-&gt; done: ApiSteps.CreateConsumption(150) (0.0s)
Then the response status must be 201
-&gt; done: ApiSteps.CheckStatus(201) (0.0s)
And the response matches schema "consumption"
-&gt; done: ApiSteps.CheckSchema("consumption") (0.0s)
And the JSON field "hasLeakSuspicion" must be true
-&gt; done: ApiSteps.CheckBoolean("hasLeakSuspicion", "true") (0.0s)
And the consumption response belongs to the created sensor
-&gt; done: ApiSteps.CheckConsumptionSensor() (0.0s)
When I list alerts
-&gt; done: ApiSteps.ListAlerts() (0.0s)
Then the response status must be 200
-&gt; done: ApiSteps.CheckStatus(200) (0.0s)
And the response matches schema "page-alerts"
-&gt; done: ApiSteps.CheckSchema("page-alerts") (0.0s)
And there must be an alert for the created sensor
-&gt; done: ApiSteps.FindAlert() (0.0s)
When I resolve the alert
-&gt; done: ApiSteps.ResolveAlert() (0.0s)
Then the response status must be 200
-&gt; done: ApiSteps.CheckStatus(200) (0.0s)
And the response matches schema "message"
-&gt; done: ApiSteps.CheckSchema("message") (0.0s)
When I list alerts again
-&gt; done: ApiSteps.ListAlertsAgain() (0.0s)
Then the response status must be 200
-&gt; done: ApiSteps.CheckStatus(200) (0.0s)
And the generated alert must be resolved
-&gt; done: ApiSteps.CheckResolvedAlert() (0.0s)</StdOut>
      </Output>
